What happens when a user types into this input?

```jsx
function Name() {
  const [name, setName] = useState('Ada');
  return <input value={name} />;
}
```

This test fails: the assertion sees an empty input. Why?

```jsx
test('types a name', () => {
  const user = userEvent.setup();
  render(<NameField />); // controlled input
  user.type(screen.getByRole('textbox'), 'hi');
  expect(screen.getByRole('textbox')).toHaveValue('hi');
});
```

A `Menu` component exposes `Menu.Item` as a static property. After wrapping it, `<Themed.Item>` is undefined. Why?

```jsx
function withTheme(Component) {
  return function Themed(props) {
    const theme = useTheme();
    return <Component {...props} theme={theme} />;
  };
}

const Themed = withTheme(Menu); // Menu.Item exists
```

What HTML does `<Box as="section" />` render?

```jsx
function Box({ as, ...rest }) {
  return <as {...rest}>x</as>;
}
```

In React 19, this HOC passes a `ref` given to `Wrapper` straight through to the wrapped function component `C`, with no `forwardRef` needed.

```jsx
function withX(C) {
  return function Wrapper(props) {
    return <C {...props} />;
  };
}
```

A test passes but prints "An update to UserCard inside a test was not wrapped in act(...)". The component fetches a user in an effect and then sets state. What is the best fix?

```jsx
test('shows the user', () => {
  render(<UserCard id="1" />);
  expect(screen.getByText('Loading…')).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

Why does the last assertion fail?

```jsx
const { result } = renderHook(() => useCounter());
const { count, increment } = result.current;

act(() => increment());
expect(count).toBe(1);
```

What is wrong with this test?

```jsx
await waitFor(() => {
  user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Add' }));
  expect(screen.getByText('Items: 1')).toBeInTheDocument();
