A form should hide its "Invalid email" message after the user fixes the field. This test passes, but the feature is broken: the message never disappears. Which change makes the test catch the bug?

```jsx
await user.type(email, 'ada@example.com');
expect(screen.queryByText('Invalid emial')).not.toBeInTheDocument();
```

Tests for components that use TanStack Query pass one at a time but fail when the whole file runs. The setup is below. What is the most likely cause and fix?

```jsx
const queryClient = new QueryClient();
const wrapper = ({ children }) => (
  <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>{children}</QueryClientProvider>
);
// each test: render(<Todos />, { wrapper })
```

Typing in this profile form loses the input's text and focus after every keystroke. Why?

```jsx
function Page({ user }) {
  const [draft, setDraft] = useState('');
  const Editor = withAutosave(ProfileEditor);
  return <Editor value={draft} onChange={setDraft} />;
}
```

A `<Modal>` renders its content with `createPortal(…, document.body)`. Why does this test fail, and what fixes it?

```jsx
const { container } = render(<Modal open />);
expect(within(container).getByRole('dialog')).toBeInTheDocument();
```

An older `<Tabs>` implementation passes state to its tabs with `cloneElement`. A consumer wraps the tabs in a layout div, and clicking a tab stops working. What is happening?

```jsx
function Tabs({ children }) {
  const [index, setIndex] = useState(0);
  return Children.map(children, (child, i) =>
    cloneElement(child, { active: i === index, onSelect: () => setIndex(i) })
  );
}

<Tabs>
  <div className="row">
    <Tab>One</Tab>
    <Tab>Two</Tab>
  </div>
</Tabs>
```

A component hides details with Tailwind's `hidden` class until "Show more" is clicked. This test passes, but in the browser the details were never hidden at all. Why?

```jsx
render(<Details />);
expect(screen.getByText('Secret')).toBeVisible();
await user.click(screen.getByRole('button', { name: 'Show more' }));
expect(screen.getByText('Secret')).toBeVisible();
```

A custom test helper mounts components with `createRoot` instead of RTL, and the global `IS_REACT_ACT_ENVIRONMENT` is `true`. What does this code observe?

```jsx
const root = createRoot(div);
root.render(<p>hello</p>);
console.log(div.textContent);
```

What is the input's value after this interaction? Type the exact text.

```jsx
render(<input aria-label="f" defaultValue="hello" />);
await user.type(screen.getByLabelText('f'), '{backspace}{backspace}X');
```

A controlled input has `maxLength={3}`. What values do these two tests see?

```jsx
